{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T05:41:36.382Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"12","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (721bde63). CONFIRMED by execution on darwin: the pre-fix walk followed a 32-link chain that darwin itself refuses (measured host limit 31), so a fixed 40-hop budget let this machine's ELOOP become a write. Fix reuses the existing linkHopLimitFor via containedLinkHopLimit rather than introducing a second notion of the limit — no separate budget was justified, since both walks expand links in userspace so the kernel's ELOOP counter never fires in either. Also adds the sticky fully-qualified-target rule mirroring agents.go (Windows 63-\u003e31). The regression test MEASURES the host limit from the kernel rather than restating the table, so it is not a tautology; on Linux the two figures coincide at 40 so it can only pass there, and it fails without the fix everywhere else. Stable over -count=3.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NC3SYGYABMB8WJ06NRVD21","targetId":"01M1NC3SYP2B970GBGT5486H2J","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC1XG2Z1PAWB1W3G44F6P7"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
